{
  "dom_id": "step-q107114",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A=\\{[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a,b,c\\in R\\}.$    \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & {b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & {b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} & 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is not a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is  *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =k[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2a & 2b \\\\ 2c & 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is  *not* closed under scalar  multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $A$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"",
